  "implementationContract": [
    "One shared actor only admits jobs, assigns a monotonic observed sequence and links each detached job to its predecessor; no synchronous file work or wait runs in admission.",
    "Order means actual admitted order, not Task creation, wall-clock call order, actor FIFO or greatest chapter/offset.",
    "save, async load, flush and sync replacement share the same process-local worker chain across store instances and books; flush waits for all predecessor jobs, with no retries or coalescing.",
    "Atomic write, success callback and success log occur in the same ordered job. Failed writes retain the existing log-only Void API and emit no onSave; later jobs still run.",
    "Accepted writes are detached from caller cancellation and finish their matching success/failure handling.",
    "Firestore's sole existing sync-import caller awaits the same writer; sync replacement intentionally never onSave/echoes a cloud push.",
    "Existing JSON path/codec and spineIndex/charOffset/translationOffset semantics are unchanged; the value type gains only Sendable."
  ],
